  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "6656296",
      "title": "Passing Parameters to Routes",
      "lectureOrder": 457,
      "videoOrder": 419,
      "sourceHash": "a48a3a6c8d88fed7a94089df231c88f8e3f5598f327a45f10a7d8e326ae48d6a",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.64,
          "end": 5.13,
          "en": "-: With the basics about routing set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.13,
          "end": 7.5,
          "en": "let's enhance our application a bit by going back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.5,
          "end": 11.43,
          "en": "to the app module and adding some other routes to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.43,
          "end": 14.79,
          "en": "Let's say that besides our user's route here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.79,
          "end": 17.61,
          "en": "we also want to be able to load a single user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.61,
          "end": 19.77,
          "en": "So to load the user component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.77,
          "end": 24.77,
          "en": "which simply well gives us that single user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.78,
          "end": 27.72,
          "en": "For that we might want to load a user dynamically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.72,
          "end": 29.67,
          "en": "because if we have a look at our user's component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.67,
          "end": 32.61,
          "en": "we see we get free users with different IDs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.61,
          "end": 35.52,
          "en": "So it would be nice if we could pass the ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.52,
          "end": 39.81,
          "en": "of the user we want to load in that route path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.81,
          "end": 41.49,
          "en": "One approach would be to set up a route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.49,
          "end": 45.42,
          "en": "with user one and then one with user two.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.42,
          "end": 49.02,
          "en": "And doesn't look very optimal because it's not very dynamic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.02,
          "end": 51.27,
          "en": "and still how would we know inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.27,
          "end": 53.88,
          "en": "of this component which route was loaded?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.88,
          "end": 56.46,
          "en": "Okay, we could harvest the path manually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.46,
          "end": 58.86,
          "en": "but that's not really a great approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.86,
          "end": 61.89,
          "en": "Instead, we can add parameters to our routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.89,
          "end": 64.92,
          "en": "dynamic segments in our paths.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.92,
          "end": 67.38,
          "en": "We do this by adding a colon,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.38,
          "end": 70.35,
          "en": "and then any name you like, like for example, ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.35,
          "end": 72.9,
          "en": "You will later be able to retrieve the parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.9,
          "end": 75.53999999999999,
          "en": "inside of the loaded component by that name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.53999999999999,
          "end": 78.81,
          "en": "You specify here, so by ID in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.81,
          "end": 81.03,
          "en": "And the colon simply tells Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.03,
          "end": 83.94,
          "en": "that this is a dynamic part of the path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.94,
          "end": 88.94,
          "en": "Without colon only routes which are user slash ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.16,
          "end": 92.13,
          "en": "and with ID, I literally mean the word ID,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.13,
          "end": 94.97999999999999,
          "en": "would lead to this component with a colon",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.97999999999999,
          "end": 98.58,
          "en": "user slash anything else would load this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 98.58,
          "end": 102.679,
          "en": "and anything else would be interpreted as the ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.679,
          "end": 107.679,
          "en": "Now with this in place, we are able to load a component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.47999999999999,
          "end": 113.47999999999999,
          "en": "the user component, with this dynamic piece sent to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.94,
          "end": 116.07,
          "en": "So if we have a look to this user component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.07,
          "end": 119.49000000000001,
          "en": "or at this user component, here we simply say user with ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 119.49000000000001,
          "end": 122.19,
          "en": "and now we simply have a dummy text here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.19,
          "end": 125.58,
          "en": "load it and user name with some dummy text here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.58,
          "end": 127.53,
          "en": "Now, for now, we won't touch this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 127.53,
          "end": 129.84,
          "en": "We won't use this parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 129.84,
          "end": 131.58,
          "en": "We will do this in the next lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.58,
          "end": 134.43,
          "en": "Let's now see if we successfully reached this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 134.43,
          "end": 137.94,
          "en": "So if we save this to let it recompile and we go back,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 137.94,
          "end": 142.94,
          "en": "we are in users, let's add slash something here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 143.94,
          "end": 146.85,
          "en": "and you see the single user component was loaded,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 146.85,
          "end": 150.15,
          "en": "the same if, if we add slash one here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 150.15,
          "end": 154.92000000000002,
          "en": "So this thing, the segment after slash users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 154.92000000000002,
          "end": 157.77,
          "en": "is indeed interpreted as dynamic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 157.77,
          "end": 161.01,
          "en": "Otherwise, we would get the error that users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 161.01,
          "end": 163.47,
          "en": "slash one is the unknown route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 163.47,
          "end": 166.47,
          "en": "It isn't because we set it up to be a known one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 166.47,
          "end": 171.09,
          "en": "because again, we added this dynamic path segment here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 171.09,
          "end": 175.44,
          "en": "Now this is how we can dynamically load some route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 175.44,
          "end": 179.1,
          "en": "how we can encode some data into our path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 179.1,
          "end": 181.71,
          "en": "How can we get access to this data in the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 181.71,
          "end": 182.85,
          "en": "loaded component though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 182.85,
          "end": 185.88,
          "en": "because that of course is another key question.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 185.88,
          "end": 188.523,
          "en": "Let's take a closer look in the next lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
